Please people - that isn't enough information to give any help.  What
do you mean "we can't even get into the game, period" - does it hang?
Does it reboot?  Do you get any error messages?  Are you running from
WorkBench or from a CLI?  Even though we are spending most of our time
these days working on the next version, we are still interested in
helping people enjoy the current one, and any bugs we find now are less
likely to survive into the next version.

Here is the generic solution: check your chip memory - you may not have
enough free.  (This is also the solution to "NetHack crashes on exit.")

This is the third time in the last few weeks I've sent out this
information.  If you find it helps, PLEASE LET US KNOW.  If you find it
doesn't help, PLEASE LET US KNOW.  If you don't tell us what's going on
in the field, we'll never know if we are or aren't solving these
problems.

